From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thehobbit85 <thehobbit85@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:44:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Document the fork touch controls so environment validation
 passes

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The fork touch-control patches add four environment settings without table rows, which makes the Tool tests job fail once it preserves test exit status
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#690
---
 docs/env_switches.tsv | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 4a8e6ef..d60abd0 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -371,7 +371,11 @@ DM_THERMAL_CAP	switch	`0` turns off the thermal cap, which holds the frame step
 DM_THR	diagnostic	`=1` logs each SVC (except `SleepThread`) with its first four arguments, and each `CreateThread` with entry, stack, priority and core
 DM_THRCPU	diagnostic	`=<tsv path>[,<seconds>]` writes each thread's CPU time (100% = one core) and the total every interval (default 10 s); on iOS a relative path is under `Documents`
 DM_TOUCH_HAPTICS	player	`0` turns off the light haptic tap when a touch control is pressed (on by default); launcher setting
+DM_TOUCH_HINT	player	Localized words for the iOS right-stick hint, shown once per launch when the 3D layout has room and no controller is connected. Empty disables the hint
+DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT	player	The player's per-layout touch-control arrangement, encoded by the shell's touch layout editor. Invalid values keep the built-in positions
 DM_TOUCH_LOG	diagnostic	`=1` logs each touch-screen read with touch points (sample, finger, position, attributes) and each gesture entry, up to 500 lines
+DM_TOUCH_SIZE	player	iOS touch-control size: small, medium (default) or large. Controls move toward medium when the requested size does not fit
+DM_TOUCH_STICK	player	iOS left touch-stick position: corner (default), higher or inward
 DM_UDC_SELFTEST	diagnostic	`=1` runs a start-up check of DontCare load and store on private depth-stencil and RGBA8 textures (clear, Load + DontCare, read back) and logs one result line
 DM_UE_SHADERS	path	Folder of the Unreal shader code archives decoded by `uepak.py`, for `shader_split.py` (default `ue_shaders` beside the RomFS); needed when the RomFS has Unreal paks
 DM_UE_TEXTURE_POOL	switch	Megabytes Unreal's texture streaming pool (`r.Streaming.PoolSize`) is raised to, overriding the profile's `ue_texture_pool`; `0` keeps the game's own pool. On iOS only this switch turns it on (`Documents/env.txt`)
